headers {
  content-type: application/json
}

auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{idToken}}
}

script:pre-request {
  // The API lives under /api/v1 (Nest global prefix + URI versioning, infra/api.ts). Environments keep the bare
  // host in `baseUrl`; every request uses `apiUrl`, so the version lives in exactly one place.
  bru.setVar("apiUrl", bru.getEnvVar("baseUrl") + "/api/v1");
}

docs {
  # Shuttle Connect API

  Every successful response is wrapped by `ResponseTransformInterceptor`:

  ```json
  { "success": true, "data": { ... } }
  ```

  Every error is shaped by `GlobalExceptionFilter`:

  ```json
  { "success": false, "error": { "code": "...", "statusCode": 400, "message": "..." } }
  ```

  So assertions read `res.body.data.*` on success and `res.body.error.code` on failure.

  ## Running the flow

  Requests are sequenced so `bru run` executes them in dependency order:
  Auth -> Courts -> Sessions -> Requests -> Host Decisions -> User. Each create step
  writes its id into an environment variable (`courtId`, `sessionId`) for the next one.

  ## Versioning

  Every route is under `/api/v1`. Environments hold the bare host in `baseUrl`; the
  pre-request script above sets `apiUrl = baseUrl + "/api/v1"`, and requests use
  `{{apiUrl}}`. See README.md -> Environments.
}
